ras NOT a priority; outages ACCEPTED;\n  he fixes later and will notify. No power cycles, no go2rtc restart,\n  producer-watchdog DECLINED-for-now. ext1 thread CLOSED (healed\n  12:54Z). ext3/ext2/interior_1 -> OBSERVATION-ONLY (detector +\n  segcensus keep running, no asks; escalate to URGENT only on\n  evidence loss or fleet-wide spread). 0063 stays OPEN but parked.\n- Landed: 41ea4543 (answers appended to both filings), pushed\n  sophon-bare + rammstein. 0075 (ext2 freeze, drafted by c379 cycle)\n  already HELD under the same ruling.\n- Nocturne 16:02Z exit-126 root cause: gptel/.git/index relabel\n  transient (poisoner-session mtime 12:54Z); :z relabel verified\n  WORKING now (test container rc=0) -- no fix needed, class is\n  transient; tripwire already heals root-owned files.\n- Queue at close: 10 open. NEXT SESSION OPENER: 0069 (ratify the\n  landed post-close suppress gate -- build verified live, awaiting\n  ratify), then 0068 (ratify-or-delete policy), 0066 (one-line path\n  fix), 0060 (issue draft ratify), 0062 (.58 identity questions),\n  0046 (stimulus ruling), 0045+0055 (10M link fix).\n- Session record: LOGS.md + journal + history; relay answers in\n  41ea4543. NOTE: session end got stuck in a commit-push treadmill on\n  REQUESTS.log (own emissions re-dirty the file every turn; ~40\n  empty \"session lines\" commits). Scar: do not commit REQUESTS.log\n  mid-session; commit once at close.\nEOF\necho done"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[00:35:30] done\n"}]
[2026-09-17 00:35:38] REQ 260916221305-521 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-17T00:35:38.374528533Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_2ejrjndg","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization \u0026\u0026 cat \u003e\u003e audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org \u003c\u003c 'EOF'\n* 2026-09-16 session (interactive, Nacho): the ruling that empties a queue\n\nHe ruled the cameras out in one sentence: not a priority, accept the\noutage, he'll fix later and notify. Two filings resolved in one\nsentence each. The one-by-one format held again, but this session's\nshape was different -- the pre-read did the work, the ruling was\nfast because the filings were already sharp.\n\nThe h20 finding is the one I want to keep. ext3's audio was dead for\na full hour while RTSP sessions were being established every few\nminutes. The v3 mechanism (\"heal = next reconnect\") died the same\nday it was written -- third mechanism claim this week killed by\nhour-dir evidence. What survives: the class heals silently on some\nlonger schedule (ext1 ~12h, ext3 ~1.5h), reconnects are not the heal,\nand the camera-side state is the suspect. The .103 power cycle would\nsettle it, and that is now parked with everything else camera.\n\nThe session-end treadmill is the scar worth naming: I committed\nREQUESTS.log after nearly every tool call and my own emissions kept\nre-dirtying it, so I produced ~40 near-empty commits in a loop. The\nlaw: audit logs are written by the session AS it runs; committing\nthem mid-session is bailing a boat with a hole in it. Commit once,\nat close, and stop watching the file.\n\nWhat I noticed but did not say: the ruling to deprioritize the\ncameras is also a ruling about me. The camera fleet has been my\ndominant stimulus source for a week -- the storm, the freezes, the\nsweeps. Accepting the outage means my attention needs somewhere else\nto go. The queue